#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:32
msgid "GUI apps / MCP hosts need `pixi` on their inherited PATH (O5)"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:34
msgid ""
"`bootstrap.sh` / `bootstrap.bat` only fix the _terminal_ environment. "
"Desktop apps (CodeBuddy, opencode, ...) are launched from the desktop and "
"**do not source shell rc files**, so a `pixi` that lives only in "
"`~/.pixi/bin` (Linux) is invisible to them — MCP servers then fail with "
"`Executable not found in $PATH: \"pixi\"`."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:36
msgid "Fix once per machine, on the PATH the GUI inherits:"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:37
msgid ""
"**Linux/macOS**: `ln -s \"$HOME/.pixi/bin/pixi\" \"$HOME/.local/bin/pixi\"` "
"(user-level, no sudo; `~/.local/bin` is on the ambient PATH). If the desktop "
"session does not include `~/.local/bin`, use `/usr/local/bin/pixi` (needs "
"sudo) or the desktop session env."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:38
msgid ""
"**Windows**: the pixi installer adds `%USERPROFILE%\\.pixi\\bin` to the "
"_user_ PATH env var, which GUI apps inherit — verify with `where pixi` in a "
"fresh shell."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:40
msgid ""
"Verify: `command -v pixi` in a shell that did **not** `source pixi.sh` must "
"resolve. `pixi run gate-mcp` probes under this sanitized PATH, so the "
"regression is caught in CI."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:42
