#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:133
msgid "CMake preset build trees (T-A0' 2026-10-10)"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:135
msgid ""
"The CMake build trees live in `cmake-build*/` (VSCode picks a preset and "
"goes). Mind the difference from the old `target/cmake-rust` shared "
"incremental surface: now **the cargo cache is isolated per build tree** "
"(PolyOrch defaults `.cargo-target/` inside each cmake-build\\*) — each "
"preset's first build compiles cargo fully once; what that buys is "
"build-directory self-sufficiency (deleting the tree = deleting everything) "
"and parallel presets. The save-frame thumbnail pipeline owns "
"`build/gallery/assets/` (wall thumbnail source), direct cargo calls own "
"`target/` exclusively."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:137
msgid ""
"Directory ownership is therefore explicit: `cmake-build*/` = configure trees "
"(one per preset), `build/gallery/assets/` = thumbnail-pipeline output, "
"`target/` = direct cargo. Nothing configures into a bare `build/` root, and "
"a stray top-level `Testing/` is ctest residue (safe to remove). The "
"committed `.vscode` debug lists are refreshed by `pixi run f5` — the `debug` "
"preset is the only tree that sees every lane (Qt on + the debug knob); no "
"other configure touches them."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:140
msgid "Qt support matrix (R2, 2026-10-15)"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:142
msgid ""
"`-DVISIAENGINE_QT=ON` resolves two generations, Qt6 preferred then Qt5: **Qt "
"6.x** (pixi `qt-spike` env, the CI lane — proven by `xvfb-run -a pixi run -e "
"qt-spike smoke-qt`) and **Qt >= 5.15** (pixi `qt5-spike` validation env, "
"conda-forge `qt 5.15.*`; validated live at 5.15.15 — discovery, E703 "
"real-window run and the ctest leg all green). **Qt 5.12 and older are "
"excluded from the contract** (owner directive 2026-10-15): the "
"`find_package(Qt5 5.15)` version arg enforces the floor and the widget "
"header carries exactly one version guard (`QMouseEvent::position()` on Qt6 "
"vs `pos()` on Qt5 — the only compile-measured divergence)."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:144
msgid ""
"Consumers never spell a generation name: the SDK publishes the canonical "
"`VISIAENGINE_QT_*` variables (FOUND / MAJOR / VERSION / TARGET / LIBDIR / "
"PLUGINSDIR — the last two probed per packaging shape, conda and Debian "
"layouts both resolve) and the example family consumes them inside "
"`visiaengine_add_example(... QT)`. The `qt5-spike` env is validation-only: "
"no solve-group, no ci chain."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/env.md:146
