#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/tutorials.md:63
msgid ""
"**The Rust E family (examples/rs) comes as a trio**: PolyOrch build handle "
"`visiaengine-example-<E#>` (mediator `visiaengine-example-<E#>-build`, the "
"D40 EXAMPLE kind -- the cargo call lives in the supplier wrapper), run step "
"`visiaengine-example-<E#>-run` (builds the handle first, then "
"polyorch_example_run executes the staged binary with the DISPLAY fallback), "
"ctest entry `example_<E#>` (runs the staged binary directly, no cargo at "
"test time) — the single home of argv is the registry in "
"`cmake/VisiaEngineBindings.cmake`, and the pixi `smoke-*` tasks are all "
"`ctest -R` forwarding shells. The cargo environment's self-sufficiency is "
"locked by the cmake-smoke state-④ triple anchor (bare PATH = IDE calls need "
"no pixi activation); per-example breakpoint debugging runs through "
"rust-analyzer Run/Debug, and with the `debug` preset on, F5 rows ride the "
"PolyOrch managed lane instead (`visiaengine-example-<E#>` launch + "
"preLaunchTask pairs)."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/tutorials.md:71
msgid ""
"**The native E family is the real thing (examples/{c,cpp,qt})**: "
"add_executable compiles what you change, one at a time, ctest entries from "
"the same source, FOLDER = the disk-directory mirror (examples/<language> "
"auto-derived; root-level steps sit bare at the top), identity semantics "
"belong to LABELS."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/tutorials.md:73
msgid ""
"**ctest**: the headless family always truly runs; the default testPreset "
"already skips the display family wholesale via `-LE display`, and the true "
"run goes through the xvfb sub-state (S4 joins the cmake-smoke display band)."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/tutorials.md:76
