#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:5
msgid "The multi-dimensional spatial visualization engine"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:7
msgid "**Version 0.1.0 | September 2026**"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:11
msgid "Abstract"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:13
msgid ""
"**VisiaEngine** is an open-source, lightweight multi-dimensional spatial "
"visualization engine. It provides a unified **2D, 2.5D and 3D rendering "
"pipeline**, purpose-built for **maps, geographic information (GIS), 3D "
"models, simulation scenes and digital-twin data**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:15
msgid ""
"VisiaEngine does not chase game-grade lighting effects; it focuses on "
"**presenting data clearly, accurately and efficiently**. Its core is "
"implemented in high-performance **Rust**, delivered in a flexible **SDK "
"shape**, embeddable in **Qt and Web** applications (Flutter/C# are roadmap "
"items), with a planned official editor, **Visia Studio**. The project "
"follows the **Open Core** model: the core runtime is permanently open "
"source, while advanced enterprise features and the editor are commercial "
"products."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:19
msgid "1. Problem and Opportunity"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:21
msgid "1.1 The split in today's market"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:22
msgid "The current visualization tooling market has a pronounced fault line:"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:23
msgid ""
"**Game engines (Unreal, Unity)**: huge footprint, weak GIS support, hard to "
"embed into ordinary desktop/Web apps, and their \"game-style\" rendering "
"habitually distracts from data visualization."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:24
msgid ""
"**GIS and Web 3D libraries (Cesium, MapLibre, deck.gl)**: good at geographic "
"data display, but most are confined to the Web stack, and deep embedding "
"into native desktop frameworks (Qt, WPF) is costly; even mature products "
"that offer 2D/2.5D/3D mode switching usually run a different scene semantic "
"per dimension, making seamless transitions over one scene tree with one "
"layer/entity semantics hard to achieve."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:25
msgid ""
"**General graphics frameworks (Three.js, Qt 3D)**: lack the layer system, "
"coordinate transforms and interaction purpose-built for spatial data; the "
"development bar is high."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:27
msgid "1.2 The unmet need"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:28
msgid ""
"Developers urgently need a **solution between the lightweight library and "
"the heavy engine**:"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:29
msgid ""
"Native support for **2D maps, the 2.5D oblique view and 3D scenes** with "
"free switching and camera flight transitions **within the same viewport**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:30
msgid ""
"Native understanding and optimization of spatial data such as **GIS "
"coordinate systems, vector tiles, and ODR high-definition roads**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:31
msgid ""
"Packageable as a lightweight SDK embedded into existing applications, yet "
"able to drive the future editor as a standalone engine."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:32
msgid ""
"Outstanding performance, cross-platform consistency, and a dependable "
"visualization base for digital twins and industrial simulation."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:36
msgid "2. What VisiaEngine Is"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:38
msgid ""
"**VisiaEngine** is a multi-dimensional visualization engine whose first goal "
"is **the clear presentation of data**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:39
msgid ""
"**Visia** is drawn from the vision word family (Latin visio, \"sight\"), "
"signifying **\"the domain of vision\"**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:40
msgid ""
"It is not a game engine and does not compete with Unreal or Unity; it "
"focuses on **turning complex spatial data into intuitive, interactive "
"views**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:42
msgid "Core creed"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:43
msgid ""
"**Visia — see the essence of your data.** _Visia — See the essence of your "
"data._"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:48
msgid "3. Core Features"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:50
msgid "3.1 A unified 2D / 2.5D / 3D core"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:51
msgid ""
"On a flat entity table (scene-tree grouping / parent-child offsets already "
"delivered: the create_group/set_parent family), switch freely between the "
"**bird's-eye map (2D)**, the **oblique view (2.5D)** and the **fully "
"immersive 3D viewport**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:52
msgid ""
"All layers, entities and annotations keep consistent interaction logic "
"across the dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:54
msgid "3.2 First-class spatial data capability"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:55
msgid ""
"**Maps and GIS**: built-in GeoJSON and mainstream coordinate-projection "
"support; vector tiles (MVT) support is delivered (Phase 0 = Rust-native "
"decode/scheduling; Phase 1 = the C API entries load_mvt_dir/set_tile_view + "
"the HTTP source \\[ureq\\], delivered in this band; WMS/WMTS raster imagery "
"is in the roadmap)."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:56
msgid ""
"**Autonomous driving and simulation**: **OpenDRIVE (ODR)** and "
"**OpenSCENARIO (OSC)** through official simulation plugins, auto-generating "
"road and traffic scenes (delivered in Beta, see the roadmap)."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:57
msgid ""
"**Models and BIM**: efficient loading of glTF, point clouds and other "
"standard formats, supporting high-fidelity lightweight display of building "
"information models."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:59
msgid "3.3 Lightweight, embeddable, high-performance"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:60
msgid "**Rust core**: memory safe, no GC, performance comparable to C++."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:61
msgid ""
"Modern rendering on **wgpu**: first-class Vulkan / Metal / DX12 / WebGPU; "
"also provides the OpenGL 3.3+ / OpenGL ES 3.0+ / WebGL2 degraded "
"compatibility tiers — what stays consistent across platforms is the API "
"surface and the quality-tier semantics; the degraded tiers trade a feature "
"subset for coverage."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:62
msgid ""
"**Delivered as an SDK**: shipped as runtime libraries (`visiaengine-core`, "
"`visiaengine-render`) over a C API for hosts such as Qt, Flutter and C# "
"(WPF/Unity), without hijacking the application main loop."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:64
msgid "3.4 Built for developers"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:65
msgid ""
"A compact, prunable modular design; the startup size can be kept **within 10 "
"MB**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:66
msgid "Clear, stable APIs backed by thorough documentation and examples."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:67
msgid ""
"Future second-development through official scripting or an extension system "
"(WebAssembly considered)."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:71
msgid "4. Technical Architecture"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:73
msgid "4.1 The core idea"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:74
msgid ""
"An architecture of **\"engine kernel + pluggable rendering backends + "
"application-layer bindings\"**."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:76
msgid ""
"```mermaid\n"
"flowchart TB\n"
"    host[\"Application layer (host)<br/>Qt / Flutter / C# / Web\"]\n"
"    core[\"visiaengine-core<br/>data model · spatial index · coordinates · "
"scene graph · resource management\"]\n"
"    render[\"visiaengine-render<br/>unified rendering abstraction<br/>(Trait "
"definitions, render-command generation)\"]\n"
"    wgpu[\"visiaengine-render-wgpu (default backend)<br/>in-house rendering "
"pipeline on wgpu\"]\n"
"    future[\"future optional backends\"]\n"
"    host -->|FFI (C API)| core --> render --> wgpu\n"
"    render -.-> future\n"
"```"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:87
msgid "4.2 Key design decisions"
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:88
msgid ""
"**Why wgpu direct, pipeline in-house?** (the 2026-09 final backend ruling) "
"wgpu provides a Rust-native modern GPU abstraction spanning "
"Vulkan/Metal/DX12/WebGPU and ships its own GL/GLES degradation backends (an "
"optional ANGLE build on Windows) — main-loop ownership, the size budget and "
"compatibility tiering can all be held by the engine. Reusing an "
"off-the-shelf engine's rendering stack (Bevy) was evaluated and not adopted: "
"its rendering layer is inseparable from its own ECS/App framework, and the "
"upstream API-stability cadence does not match an SDK's long-term "
"compatibility promise. The `visiaengine-render` abstraction layer stays: "
"future optional backends (a mobile-exclusive or an enterprise customization, "
"say) still join through the same C API compatibility discipline."
msgstr ""

#: /home/ubuntu/Documents/VisiaEngine/build/i18n-src/docs/whitepaper.md:89
msgid ""
"**How are 2D/2.5D/3D unified?** All visual primitives (points, lines, faces, "
"volumes) exist as spatial entities; perspective/orthographic projections "
"switch freely and bird's-eye/oblique camera flights need no renderer swap. "
"(The continuously interpolated projection morph between viewpoints is "
"delivered: the `set_morph_time` continuous slider, E304.)"
msgstr ""

